Trigger A Pod Recovery By Killing Process On Vdu
    [Arguments]  ${pod_name}  ${container_name}  ${process_name}=ministarter  ${conn_prompt}=${EMPTY}  ${vdu_index}=0    ${gnb_index}=0
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to trigger a given vdu pod restart by kill a process in container.
    ...  The keyword includes ssh connection and disconnection to OE.
    ...
    ...  ``kubectl exec -it <full pod name> -c <full container name> -- pkill ministarter``
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    | =Input Parameters= | =Man= | =Description= |
    ...    | pod_name | Yes | The abbreviated name of the pod with pod index, or full pod name, like l2rt-0, po-cran1-l2nrt-0 |
    ...    | container_name | Yes | The abbreviated name of the container. |
    ...    | process_name | Yes | The process name that needs to be killed, default is ministarter. |
    ...    | conn_prompt | No | The prompt of ssh connection to OE. |
    ...    | vdu_index | No | vdu index in testline configuration file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | gnb_index | No | gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...
    ...   *Example:*
    ...   | Trigger vDU Pod Retart By Killing Process | pod_name=po-cran1-l2nrt-0 | container_name=l2hi |
    ...
    ${alias}    generic_utils.get_unique_id_string
    ${ns}   tl_config.get_vdu_namespace
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ssh_conn.connect_to_vdu_cloud_hosting
    ...  using_tenant=${True}
    ...  prompt=${conn_prompt}
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ...  alias=${alias}
    vdu_cli_base.execute_vdu_pod_restart_by_killing_process
    ...  pod_name=${pod_name}
    ...  container_name=${container_name}
    ...  namespace=${ns}
    ...  process_name=${process_name}
    ...  conn_alias=${alias}
    [Teardown]   ssh_conn.disconnect_vdu_cloud_hosting   alias=${alias}

Trigger A Random N+ Pods Recovery By Killing Process On Vdu
    [Arguments]  ${pod_abbr}  ${container_abbr}  ${process_name}=ministarter  ${conn_prompt}=${EMPTY}  ${vdu_index}=0    ${gnb_index}=0
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to trigger a random N+ pods restart by kill a process in container.
    ...  Firstly, a random N+ pod will be selected, and then kill the given process using the next command,
    ...
    ...  ``kubectl exec -it <full pod name> -c <full container name> -- pkill ministarter``
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    | =Input Parameters= | =Man= | =Description= |
    ...    | pod_abbr | Yes | The abbreviated name of the pod. |
    ...    | container_abbr | Yes | The abbreviated name of the container. |
    ...    | process_name | Yes | The process name that needs to be killed, default is ministarter. |
    ...    | conn_prompt | No | The prompt of ssh connection to OE. |
    ...    | vdu_index | No | vdu index in testline configuration file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | gnb_index | No | gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...
    ...   *Example:*
    ...   | Trigger A Random N+ Pods Recovery By Killing Process On Vdu | pod_abbr=l2nrt | container_name=l2hi |
    ...
    ${random_pod_name}=    _Select Random Pod
    ...  pod_abbr=${pod_abbr}
    ...  conn_prompt=${conn_prompt}
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}

    Trigger A Pod Recovery By Killing Process On Vdu
    ...  pod_name=${random_pod_name}
    ...  container_name=${container_abbr}
    ...  process_name=${process_name}
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}

Trigger A Certain Type Of Pods Recovery By Killing Process On Vdu
    [Arguments]  ${pod_abbr}    ${container_abbr}   ${process_name}=ministarter  ${conn_prompt}=${EMPTY}  ${vdu_index}=0    ${gnb_index}=0
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to trigger a certain type of vdu pods recovery by killing process in all pods of this type.
    ...  The keyword includes ssh connection and disconnection to OE.
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    | =Input Parameters= | =Man= | =Description= |
    ...    | pod_abbr | Yes | The abbreviated name of the pod, like ahm |
    ...    | container_abbr | Yes | The abbreviated name of the container. |
    ...    | process_name | Yes | The process name that needs to be killed, default is ministarter. |
    ...    | conn_prompt | No | The prompt of ssh connection to OE. |
    ...    | vdu_index | No | vdu index in testline configuration file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | gnb_index | No | gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...
    ...   *Example:*
    ...   | Trigger A Certain Type Of Pods Recovery By Killing Process On Vdu | pod_abbr=l2rt | container_abbr=l2rt |
    ...
    ${alias}    generic_utils.get_unique_id_string
    ${ns}   tl_config.get_vdu_namespace
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ssh_conn.connect_to_vdu_cloud_hosting
    ...  using_tenant=${True}
    ...  prompt=${conn_prompt}
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ...  alias=${alias}
    ${target_pods_name}    vdu_cli_base.get_all_pods_name_of_one_certain_type   ns=${ns}   pod_abbr=${pod_abbr}   alias=${alias}
    FOR  ${pod_name}  IN  @{target_pods_name}
        vdu_cli_base.execute_vdu_pod_restart_by_killing_process
        ...  pod_name=${pod_name}
        ...  container_name=${container_abbr}
        ...  namespace=${ns}
        ...  process_name=${process_name}
        ...  conn_alias=${alias}
    END
    [Teardown]   ssh_conn.disconnect_vdu_cloud_hosting   alias=${alias}

Trigger Pods Recovery By Deleting All Pods Of A Certain Type On Vdu
    [Arguments]  ${pod_abbr}    ${conn_prompt}=${EMPTY}  ${vdu_index}=0    ${gnb_index}=0
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to trigger a certain type of vdu pods recovery by deleting all pods of this type.
    ...  The keyword includes ssh connection and disconnection to OE.
    ...
    ...  ``kubectl get pods -n <namespace>|egrep "(<pod_abbr>)" |awk '{print $1}'|xargs kubectl delete pod -n <namespace>``
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    | =Input Parameters= | =Man= | =Description= |
    ...    | pod_abbr | Yes | The abbreviated name of the pod, like ahm |
    ...    | conn_prompt | No | The prompt of ssh connection to OE. |
    ...    | vdu_index | No | vdu index in testline configuration file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | gnb_index | No | gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...
    ...   *Example:*
    ...   | Trigger Pods Recovery By Deleting All Pods Of A Certain Type On Vdu | pod_abbr=ahm |
    ...
    ${alias}    generic_utils.get_unique_id_string
    ${ns}   tl_config.get_vdu_namespace
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ssh_conn.connect_to_vdu_cloud_hosting
    ...  using_tenant=${True}
    ...  prompt=${conn_prompt}
    ...  vdu_index=${vdu_index}
    ...  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ...  alias=${alias}
    ssh_conn.execute_normal_cmd
    ...  base_command=kubectl get pods
    ...  namespace=${ns}
    ...  pipe_cmd=|egrep "(${pod_abbr})" |awk '{print $1}'|xargs kubectl delete pod -n ${ns}
    ...  alias=${alias}
    [Teardown]   ssh_conn.disconnect_vdu_cloud_hosting   alias=${alias}


vDU Cells Status Should Be As Expected
    [Arguments]  ${cells_id_list}  ${vdu_index}=0    ${gnb_index}=0   ${webem_password}=${EMPTY}
    ...   ${administrative_state}=Unlocked  ${operational_state}=enabled
    ...   ${availability_status}=on line  ${blocking_state}=Unblocked
    ...   ${log_level}=DEBUG   ${procedural_status}=${None}
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check specified vdu cell status should be as expected.
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* lingting.sun@nokia-sbell.com
    ...    *Change History*
    ...    | date | who | waht or how |
    ...    | 2023-12-29 | chris.l.cao | add procedural_status parameter |
    ...
    ...    | =Input Parameters= | =Man= | =Description= |
    ...    | cells_id_list | Yes | vdu cell id  list, [1, 2, 3]  |
    ...    | vdu_index     | No  | vdu index in testline configuration file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | gnb_index     | No  | gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | webem_password | No | default value is EMPTY will get from file init |
    ...    | administrative_state | No | Expected administrative state for cell, default is Unlocked |
    ...    | operational_state    | No | Expected operational_state for cell, default is Unlocked |
    ...    | availability_status  | No | Expected availability_status for cell, default is Unlocked |
    ...    | blocking_state       | No | Expected blocking_state for cell, default is Unlocked |
    ...    | procedural_status    | No | Expected procedural_status for cell, default is ${None} |
    ...
    ...    *RETURN VALUE*
    ...    None
    ...
    ...    Example
    ...    |  vDU Cells Status Should Be As Expected  |  [1,2,3]  |   administrative_state=Unlocked  |
    ${unexpected}  set variable  ${False}
    ${conn_alias}    generic_utils.get_unique_id_string
    vdu_gen.login_rest   vdu_index=${vdu_index}   gnb_index=${gnb_index}   alias=${conn_alias}   webem_password=${webem_password}
    ${cells_status_info}   vdu_ope_business.get_vdu_all_cells_status  conn_alias=${conn_alias}
    FOR    ${cell_id}    IN    @{cells_id_list}
        ${r}  run keyword and continue on failure  generic_utils.member_should_not_contain
        ...  condition_key=id  condition_value=${cell_id}  info_list=${cells_status_info}  log_level=${log_level}
        ...  administrative_state=${administrative_state}  operational_state=${operational_state}
        ...  availability_status=${availability_status}  blocking_state=${blocking_state}
        ...  procedural_status=${procedural_status}
    ${unexpected}    evaluate   ${unexpected} or ${r}
    END
    Should Not Be True  ${unexpected}  msg=Has cell with unexpected status, please check the error message!!
    [Teardown]    vdu_gen.logout_rest    conn_alias=${conn_alias}


